{
  "id": "80716",
  "type": "Page",
  "tags": [],
  "title": "Average Reaction Rate",
  "content": {
    "bibrefs": [],
    "model": [
      {
        "children": [
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "A rate is a measure of how some property varies with time. Speed is a familiar rate that expresses the distance an object travels in a given amount of time. Wage is a rate that represents the amount of money a person earns by working for a given amount of time. Likewise, the rate of a chemical reaction—its "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "reaction rate"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Measure of the speed at which a chemical reaction takes place."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2459481011",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": "—is a measure of how much reactant is consumed or how much product is produced by the reaction in a given amount of time."
              }
            ],
            "id": "s95y7i509akskuj",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Reaction rates are determined by measuring the time dependence of some property that can be related to "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "reactant"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Substance undergoing a chemical or physical change; shown on the left side of the arrow in a chemical equation."
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "1198111054",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3049743138",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " or "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "product"
                  }
                ],
                "content": [
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "Substance formed by a chemical or physical change; shown on the right side of the arrow in a chemical equation. "
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "2014122047",
                    "type": "p"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "1580957654",
                "trigger": "hover",
                "type": "popup"
              },
              {
                "text": " concentrations. For example, the rates of reactions that consume or produce gaseous substances are determined by measuring changes in volume or pressure. If a reaction involves aqueous electrolytes, rates can be measured by changes in a solution’s conductivity. For reactions involving one or more colored substances, such as in the following example, rates can be determined by measuring light absorption at intervals over a given period of time."
              }
            ],
            "id": "obundtiao0erxay",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Let’s consider how the reactant and product concentrations change over time for the general reaction A "
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": ""
                  }
                ],
                "legacyBlockRendered": false,
                "src": "\\rightarrow",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula_inline"
              },
              {
                "text": " B. As the reaction proceeds, we see that the color of the solution fades as the concentration of the violet-colored reactant A decreases. Although we cannot see it, the concentration of the colorless product B increases."
              }
            ],
            "id": "pdssj07y6g055ka",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "alt": "The reaction A arrow pointing right B is shown on the left. violet is under A and colorless is under B. On the right a graph is shown with \n            the label, “Time ( min ),” appearing on the x-axis and “Concentration ( capital M )” on the y-axis. The x-axis markings begin at 0 and end at 2. \n            The markings are labeled at intervals of 0.5. The y-axis begins at 0 and includes markings every 0.02, up to 0.10. A decreasing, concave up, \n            non-linear curve is shown in violet, which begins at 0.10 on the y-axis and reaches a value near 0 at the far right of the graph. An increasing, \n            concave down, non-linear curve is shown in gray, which begins at 0.0 on the y-axis and reaches a value near 0.10 at the far right of the graph. \n            Five beakers containing small violet and gray circles are shown above the graph. The beaker above 0 min contains 24 violet circles. The beaker \n            above 0.5 min contains 12 violet and 12 gray circles. The beaker above 1.0 min contains 6 violet and 18 gray circles. The beaker above 1.5 min \n            contains 3 violet and 21 gray circles. The beaker above 2.0 min contains 1 violet and 23 gray circles.",
            "caption": [
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "em": true,
                    "text": "As the reaction proceeds, the concentration of reactant A (violet) decreases and the concentration of product B (colorless) increases, causing color of the solution to fade. "
                  }
                ],
                "id": "3228227791",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "xlciwrmhca2rjml",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "2lvmwtp9yqqr21g",
            "src": "https://d2xvti2irp4c7t.cloudfront.net/media/bb/bb3c7d4dd01bd9764ee676f509b0bb03/A_B_graph.png",
            "type": "img",
            "width": "700"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The reaction rate at any point during the reaction can be expressed in terms of the change of either A or B with respect to time. The average rate of change of the product B, given over a particular time interval, is:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "fp4smbg0d5pfs8t",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "gp3mw26z4em0mii",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "glhz4ldlt4dldm8",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\frac{\\mathrm{change}\\;\\mathrm{in}\\;\\mathrm{concentration}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm B}{\\mathrm{change}\\;\\mathrm{in}\\;\\mathrm{time}}\\; =\\;\\frac{{\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}_{\\mathrm{final}}\\;-\\;{\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}_{\\mathrm{initial}}}{t_{\\mathrm{final}}\\;-\\;t_{\\mathrm{initial}}} =\\;\\frac{{\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}_{t_2}\\;-\\;{\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}_{t_1}}{t_2\\;-\\;t_1}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]} {\\mathrm\\Delta t}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "The brackets indicate concentration, which is usually in units of molarity. [B]"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "sub": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "doublesub": true,
                "text": "1"
              },
              {
                "text": " represents the concentration of B at some time "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "1"
              },
              {
                "text": ", and [B]"
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "sub": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "doublesub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": " is the concentration at a later time "
              },
              {
                "em": true,
                "text": "t"
              },
              {
                "sub": true,
                "text": "2"
              },
              {
                "text": ". The symbol delta (Δ) indicates “change in.” Note that B is being produced, and its rate of appearance is positive:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "b28pts5233s2mkr",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "0xlv6bgx23ftwj2",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "40769665",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm{appearance}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm B\\;=\\;\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack\\mathrm B\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Similarly, the average rate of change of the reactant A is:"
              }
            ],
            "id": "p5xasl6mzfy90n7",
            "src": "\\frac{\\mathrm{change}\\;\\mathrm{in}\\;\\mathrm{concentration}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm A}{\\mathrm{change}\\;\\mathrm{in}\\;\\mathrm{time}}\\;\\; =\\;\\frac{{\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}_{\\mathrm{final}}\\;-\\;{\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}_{\\mathrm{initial}}}{t_{\\mathrm{final}}\\;-\\;t_{\\mathrm{initial}}} =\\;\\frac{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_{t_2}\\;-\\;{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_{t_1}}{t_2\\;-\\;t_1}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack} {\\mathrm\\Delta t}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "bp57a41lf1b4e6z",
                "text": " ",
                "type": "text"
              }
            ],
            "id": "l8khc9uo6avd07r",
            "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
            "src": "\\frac{\\mathrm{change}\\;\\mathrm{in}\\;\\mathrm{concentration}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm A}{\\mathrm{change}\\;\\mathrm{in}\\;\\mathrm{time}}\\;\\; =\\;\\frac{{\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}_{\\mathrm{final}}\\;-\\;{\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}_{\\mathrm{initial}}}{t_{\\mathrm{final}}\\;-\\;t_{\\mathrm{initial}}} =\\;\\frac{{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_{t_2}\\;-\\;{\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}_{t_1}}{t_2\\;-\\;t_1}\\;=\\;\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack} {\\mathrm\\Delta t}",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": "Because the concentration of the reactant A decreases as the reaction proceeds, Δ[A] is a negative quantity, and the rate of change of A is a negative number. Rates of reaction are, by convention, expressed as positive quantities: "
              }
            ],
            "id": "gxyg9pai0lcp921",
            "type": "p"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "id": "g6d0ngsdg835mi9",
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "3938781395",
            "src": "\\mathrm{Rate}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm{disappearance}\\;\\mathrm{of}\\;\\mathrm A\\;=\\;-\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\;=\\;\\left|\\frac{\\mathrm\\Delta\\lbrack\\mathrm A\\rbrack}{\\mathrm\\Delta t}\\right|",
            "subtype": "latex",
            "type": "formula"
          },
          {
            "children": [
              {
                "text": ""
              }
            ],
            "id": "3409858583",
            "type": "p"
          }
        ],
