              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "Use this data to calculate the average reaction rate for both A and B during the time interval from 1.000 to 1.500 min."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "739796938",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The average rate of appearance of B from 1.000 min to 1.500 min is:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vjbl04z09qni1jk",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "ii45s50l9seuzag",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "xmbz1ouydf6i5yv",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\frac{\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm B\\right]}{\\Delta t}\\;=\\;\\frac{(0.0875\\;\\mathrm M\\;-\\;0.0750\\;\\mathrm M)}{(1.500\\;\\min\\;-\\;1.000\\;\\min)}\\; =\\;0.0250\\;\\mathrm M/\\min",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "During the same time interval, the average rate of disappearance of A is:"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "8ptsu1d2lt21f93",
                "type": "p"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "id": "m1oska6wt6a1v56",
                    "text": " ",
                    "type": "text"
                  }
                ],
                "id": "vz7gvgl6tn3fjdc",
                "legacyBlockRendered": "true",
                "src": "\\frac{\\Delta\\left[\\mathrm A\\right]}{\\Delta t}=-\\frac{(0.0125\\;\\mathrm M-0.0250\\;\\mathrm M)}{(1.500\\;\\min-1.000\\;\\min)}=-\\left(-\\;0.0250\\;\\mathrm M/\\min\\right)=\\;0.0250\\;\\mathrm M/\\min",
                "subtype": "latex",
                "type": "formula"
              },
              {
                "children": [
                  {
                    "text": "The rate of change of A is negative. We place a negative sign in front of this expression because reaction rates are expressed as positive quantities. Note that because this reaction has 1:1 "
                  },
                  {
                    "children": [
                      {
                        "text": "stoichiometry"
                      }
                    ],
                    "content": [
                      {
                        "children": [
                          {
                            "text": "Relationships between the amounts of reactants and products of a chemical reaction. "
                          }
                        ],
                        "id": "1666178130",
                        "type": "p"
                      }
                    ],
                    "id": "258390598",
                    "trigger": "hover",
                    "type": "popup"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": ", A and B have the same magnitude for their rates of change."
                  }
                ],
                "id": "gyoo135ys0mejpz",
                "type": "p"
              }
            ],
